# 9. Principal risks and mitigations

| Risk | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| Incorrect legal classification | Function-based analysis, conservative interim treatment, counsel review |
| Misallocated provider/deployer duties | Architecture- and conduct-based role matrix |
| Customer rubber-stamps outputs | UX controls, training, authority requirements, monitoring |
| Disparate impact | Job-specific validation, lawful testing, monitoring, appeals |
| Localization or transfer failure | Data-class mapping, routing evidence, support and subprocessor controls |
| Unsupported marketing claims | Claims library, substantiation records, controlled distribution |
| Product fragmentation | Shared baseline, policy packs, feature gates, common UX |
| Regulatory change | Legal-date register, regulatory library, quarterly review |
| Customer misuse | Due diligence, acceptable-use rules, monitoring, suspension rights |
| Inadequate evidence | Release gates, version control, independent assurance |
| Sensitive-data risk | Global prohibition or tightly controlled approval |
| Data-reuse disputes | Default prohibition on shared-model training, tenant isolation, deletion controls |
| Excessive deployment complexity | Customer-controlled deployment as an exception |
| Configuration drift | Technical enforcement, monitoring, recertification, suspension |
| Conflicting country requirements | Counsel-validated overlays, regional workflows, conflict escalation |
| Insufficient capacity | Funded staffing plan, priority-market sequencing, unsupported-scope decisions |
| Reputational harm from one deployment | Customer segmentation, activation review, monitoring, incident response |

