Global People will maintain a controlled country addendum for each country. No country may launch this policy, a material role restriction, or a flexible-work pilot until the policy register records:

- country Legal and HR approval;
- completion of required works-council, union, or employee-representative processes;
- required Payroll, Finance, Privacy, Security, Tax, Immigration, and Occupational Health review;
- covered employee categories and roles;
- effective date;
- assumptions and limitations;
- unresolved risks and owners;
- next review date.

Each country addendum must define:

- permitted work patterns and role categories;
- maximum working time, breaks, and rest;
- overtime authorization, recording, payment, and time off;
- ordinary availability, on-call, standby, call-out, and emergency work;
- right-to-disconnect requirements;
- consultation, notification, consent, and approval requirements;
- home-working health and safety;
- equipment, connectivity, ergonomic, and expense rules;
- public holidays, leave, and religious observance;
- accommodation procedures;
- privacy, monitoring, recording, and data-transfer rules;
- payroll, tax, immigration, and social-security requirements;
- approved work locations and cross-border-work rules;
- client, regulatory, security, and licensing restrictions;
- local complaint and appeal routes;
- language and accessibility requirements.

Country differences must be explained in plain language to affected employees.

