| Saudi Arabia | 3 | Later Gulf scale market | Significant potential and growing digital-finance adoption | Arabic-first operations, local partnerships, data and licensing |
| Qatar | 3–4 | Affluent niche | Strong banking penetration and institutional opportunities | Small market and conservative adoption |
| Oman | 3–4 | Selective niche | Growing digital finance and Islamic-finance opportunities | Smaller scale and cautious adoption |
| Kuwait | 3–4 | Partnership-led niche | Wealthy, bank-centered customer base | Conservative adoption and regulatory complexity |

### 2026 base case

1. Complete Malaysia readiness and conduct a limited pilot only if all gates pass.
2. Complete Indonesia preparation; launch only if low-ticket economics and controls are proven.
3. Prepare UAE and Bahrain partnerships without committing to customer launch.
4. Defer broad Saudi, Qatar, Oman and Kuwait entry.

### 2026 upside case

1. Malaysia controlled pilot.
2. Indonesia controlled pilot.
3. One Gulf pilot—UAE or Bahrain—after an independent readiness review.

